  "body": "### Summary\nAs a user, I want the app's background requests to reuse the connection the forum session already has, so that a check or a flag write does not pay a new TCP + TLS handshake next to the page I am waiting for. Audit #1388, findings B4, B9, B10. This is the \"connection reuse\" lead (2) of #1375, with the code evidence; fix it there or here, not twice.\n\n### Findings (read at `dev-swift` `1685bcc`; request counts measured with a scripted transport, handshake cost not measured)\n1. **A probe is a new `HFRSession` with 2 new `URLSession`s and an empty connection pool, on every call** (`Packages/HFRKit/Sources/HFRNetwork/Session/HFRSession.swift:85-87`, `:62-68`): `SessionRefreshFlow.refresh` (`:47`), `MPUnreadPoll.unreadCount` (`:58`), `LoginFlow.login` (`:29`, `:46`), `OwnSmileysFlow` (`:32`), `SmileyLookupFlow` (`:44`). Launch with N accounts: N profile checks on N cold connections, next to the first visible load.\n2. **Every gated write runs a fresh session check first, with no reuse of a recent verdict** (`TopicFlagFlow.swift:181-202`; also `PollVoteFlow.swift:102`). Measured: add favourite = 1 check GET + 1 write; 3 refreshes in a row = 3 probes. Removing 5 favourites = 10 requests, 5 on new sessions. Legacy: 1 request per write. The check is deliberate (#314, #1200): **only reusing a `valid` verdict for a short window, keyed on the login generation, is proposed, and that is a security trade-off for the operator to accept before any code.**\n3. **`PageFetcher.init` builds a fresh `AnonymousTransport()` by default** (`PageFetcher.swift:15`): 2 more `URLSession`s per fetcher (`AnonymousTransport.swift:21`), per environment in `AppEnvironment.swift:48` and per call in `UserProfileSource.swift:34`, `MPCheckForum.swift:37`, `OwnSmileysFlow.swift:35`. `URLSessionTransport.deinit` invalidates only the no-redirect twin (`URLSessionTransport.swift:19-21`): the main session it created is never invalidated (whether that leaks is not verified).\n4. **The AQ feed is read 3 s after every root build** (`RootNavigationView.swift:49`, `QualityAlertsModel.swift:123-128`): at launch, and again on each account switch, login, logout and for each window. Legacy reads it once at launch (`MainWindow.swift:1609` @ `87fe0d1c`). The feed does not depend on the account; only the hidden-category rule does.\n\n### Proposed fix\n- One long-lived probe transport per account (jar reset per use), or the probe sent on the account's own `URLSession` with an explicit `Cookie` header and cookie handling off.\n- One shared `AnonymousTransport`; invalidate a main session the transport created.\n- AQ count: once per launch and when the list is shown; a rebuilt root reuses the last feed.\n- The verdict reuse of point 2 only on the operator's go.\n\n### Tests\nEngine: a counter on probe creation (a `package` seam) → a refresh, a poll and a gated write create no new `URLSession`. App: two root builds → one AQ feed request.\n\nSessions and auth: merged by the core orchestrator or the maintainer (AGENTS.md §8).\n\nRefs #1388, #1375.",
