   "body": "/claim cloud/i1398-opus\n\nPlan (points 1, 3, 4; point 2, the verdict reuse, stays out until the operator's go):\n- Point 1: each account `HFRSession` keeps a small pool of probe connections (`URLSession` + its own jar). A probe stays a fresh `HFRSession` (no `hash_check`, generation 0, jar emptied then seeded with the given cookies), but its `URLSession` is recycled when the probe is released, so a refresh, a poll or a gated write's check stops opening a new connection each time. Isolation kept: two concurrent probes never share a jar; a connection whose last exchange failed or was cancelled is never recycled.\n- Point 3: one shared `AnonymousTransport` (default of `PageFetcher` and the other defaults); `URLSessionTransport` invalidates the main session it created itself.\n- Point 4: the AQ feed is read once per launch (and when the list is shown); a rebuilt root reuses it.\n- Tests: an engine counter of created `URLSession`s → N refreshes of one account create one probe connection; app test: two root builds → one AQ request.\n- No change to `AccountsModel` or the refresh flow's decisions (coordination with #1390 on #893).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
   "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
